# Keep our de-Lovabled versions of these files on merges from a Lovable upstream.
# Requires the local "ours" merge driver to be registered once:
#   git config merge.ours.driver true
# (scripts/setup-merge-drivers.sh does this for you)
# Lovable's scratch plan file was removed from this fork; upstream keeps editing
# it, which conflicts on every merge.
#
# NOTE: merge=ours does NOT keep these deleted, despite what this line looks
# like it promises. A merge driver only resolves CONTENT conflicts. Upstream
# adding a new file under .lovable/ is not a conflict, and a delete/modify pair
# is a tree-level conflict the driver never sees — so the files come back.
# Verified in practice. The actual enforcement is the "Re-remove .lovable/"
# step in .github/workflows/sync-upstream.yml. This entry is kept only for the
# case where both sides modified the same tracked file.
.lovable/** merge=ours
vite.config.ts merge=ours
bunfig.toml merge=ours
.env.example merge=ours
.gitignore merge=ours

# Force LF for anything CI executes. Relying on each contributor having
# core.autocrlf set is not a guarantee; a CRLF shebang fails on Linux with
#   /usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory
*.sh text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
